{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"printf '%s\n' '--- spec ---' && sed -n '1,260p' attest/specs/151/spec.md && printf '%s\n' '--- rulings ---' && sed -n '1,320p' attest/rulings.md && printf '%s\n' '--- criteria ---' && for f in attest/specs/151/criteria/*.sh; do printf '\\\\n### %s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' \\\"\"'$f\"; done && printf '\"'%s\n' '--- diff summary ---' && git apply --stat /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp7az7hilq/diff.patch && printf '%s\n' '--- diff relevant file headers ---' && rg -n '\"'^diff --git |''^@@|stream_line_events|claude-code|STOP_CLASSES|started|recover|stall_after'\"' /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp7az7hilq/diff.patch | head -n 500\"","aggregated_output":"--- spec ---\n## Problem\n\nAn invocation that begins and does not end leaves nothing. On 2026-09-17 two build attempts of item #148 died between passing their gates and writing their record: the first with its spawning process, the second under a live one; each left a worktree holding an unrecorded executor commit, no record, no stop, and no line anywhere the product owns. `attavo doctor` held on both, because every proof reads records and a dead invocation writes none; the operator screen rendered the row from the last record and so showed a failed attempt as the whole truth while nothing ran; recovery was three hand-written shell blocks. The product has no primitive for \"this invocation began\", so nothing can say \"and it did not end\".\n\nRetires: the by-hand recovery of a dead or hung drive (the worktree removed, the branch reset, the events archived by a person); the screen's in-memory notion of a running drive as the only witness that one runs; silence as an outcome.\n\n## Claims\n\n- bin/attavo\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- attavo.toml\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n- tests/test_drive.py\n- tests/test_ledger.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh: on a fixture tenant with a build-01.started marker naming a dead pid on this host and no build-01.json, attavo doctor --json fails proof no-invocation-lacks-record naming build-01, and holds once build-01.json exists\n- recover-writes-a-died-record.sh: on the same fixture, attavo drive --recover 1 writes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died, provenance product, with a log beside it, committed by the driver identity with a clean tree, after which proof five holds\n- died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh: both stage schemas' stop enums name died and hung, the manifest schema declares [drive].stall_after_s, and bin/attavo's STOP_CLASSES names both\n--- rulings ---\n# Rulings\n\nWritten by the merge of a proposed amendment only.\n--- criteria ---\n\n### attest/specs/151/criteria/died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor stage in (\"build\", \"verify\"):\n    enum = json.load(open(f\"schema/records/{stage}.schema.json\"))[\"properties\"][\"stop\"][\"properties\"][\"class\"][\"enum\"]\n    assert \"died\" in enum and \"hung\" in enum, (stage, enum)\ndrive = json.load(open(\"schema/manifest.schema.json\"))[\"properties\"][\"drive\"]\nassert \"stall_after_s\" in drive[\"properties\"], drive\nPY\ngrep -q '\"died\", \"hung\"' bin/attavo\n\n### attest/specs/151/criteria/doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$tmp\"\ngit init -q -b main .\ngit config user.email doctor@attavo.invalid\ngit config user.name \"doctor fixture\"\nprintf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[drive]\\nstall_after_s = 60\\n' > attavo.toml\ngit add attavo.toml\ngit commit -q -m install\nmkdir -p records/1\nsleep 0 &\ndead=$!\nwait \"$dead\"\npython3 - \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.started\" \"$dead\" <<'PY'\nimport json, socket, sys\njson.dump({\"at\": \"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\", \"host\": socket.gethostname(), \"pid\": int(sys.argv[2]),\n           \"sha\": \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\", \"product_version\": \"fixture\"},\n          open(sys.argv[1], \"w\"))\nPY\ngit add records\ngit commit -q -m \"invocation marker for item 1\"\ncd \"$here\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor-without.json\" || true\nprintf '{\"status\": \"pass\"}' > \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.json\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" > \"$tmp/doctor-with.json\" || true\npython3 - \"$tmp/doctor-without.json\" \"$tmp/doctor-with.json\" <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\ndef proof(path):\n    d = json.load(open(path))\n    return [x for x in d[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"] == \"no-invocation-lacks-record\"][0]\nwithout = proof(sys.argv[1])\nassert without[\"holds\"] is False, without\nassert \"build-01\" in without[\"reason\"] and \"never wrote its record\" in without[\"reason\"], without\nwith_record = proof(sys.argv[2])\nassert with_record[\"holds\"] is True, with_record\nPY\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n\n### attest/specs/151/criteria/recover-writes-a-died-record.sh\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\nhere=$(pwd)\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\ncd \"$tmp\"\ngit init -q -b main .\ngit config user.email person@attavo.invalid\ngit config user.name \"recover fixture\"\nprintf '[paths]\\nrecords = \"records\"\\n\\n[drive]\\nstall_after_s = 60\\n\\n[executor]\\nbuild = \"fixture\"\\n' > attavo.toml\ngit add attavo.toml\ngit commit -q -m install\ngit checkout -q -b attavo/1-x\nmkdir -p records/1\nsleep 0 &\ndead=$!\nwait \"$dead\"\npython3 - \"$tmp/records/1/build-01.started\" \"$dead\" <<'PY'\nimport json, socket, sys\njson.dump({\"at\": \"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\", \"host\": socket.gethostname(), \"pid\": int(sys.argv[2]),\n           \"sha\": \"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\", \"product_version\": \"fixture\"},\n          open(sys.argv[1], \"w\"))\nPY\ngit add records\ngit commit -q -m \"invocation marker for item 1\"\npython3 \"$here/bin/attavo\" drive --recover 1\ntest -f records/1/build-01.json\ntest -f records/1/build-01.log\npython3 - records/1/build-01.json <<'PY'\nimport json, sys\nr = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\nassert r[\"status\"] == \"failed\", r\nassert r[\"stop\"][\"class\"] == \"died\" and r[\"stop\"][\"provenance\"] == \"product\", r[\"stop\"]\nassert \"wrote no build-01.json\" in r[\"stop\"][\"detail\"], r[\"stop\"]\nPY\ntest \"$(git log -1 --format=%an)\" = \"attavo driver\"\ntest -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\"\ncd \"$here\"\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \"$tmp\" | python3 -c 'import json,sys; p=[x for x in json.load(sys.stdin)[\"proofs\"] if x[\"proof\"]==\"no-invocation-lacks-record\"][0]; assert p[\"holds\"] is True, p'\nrm -rf \"$tmp\"\n--- diff summary ---\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-CLKDGzcp' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-CXNe24Jr' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n attest/records/151/approval-01.json                |   10 \n attest/records/151/build-01.filed                  |    1 \n attest/records/151/build-01.json                   |   45 \n attest/records/151/build-01.log                    |  353 ++\n attest/records/151/counsel-01.json                 |   54 \n attest/records/151/counsel-01.log                  |   17 \n attest/records/151/spec-01.json                    |   29 \n .../151/criteria/died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh |   11 \n ...doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh |   39 \n .../151/criteria/recover-writes-a-died-record.sh   |   39 \n attest/specs/151/spec.md                           |   22 \n attest/specs/151/stub/attavo.toml                  |   51 \n attest/specs/151/stub/bin/attavo                   | 3662 ++++++++++++++++++++\n attest/specs/151/stub/bin/attavo.orig              | 3392 ++++++++++