ktree removed, the branch reset, the events archived by a person); the screen's in-memory notion of a running drive as the only witness that one runs; silence as an outcome.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- bin/attavo\\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\\n- attavo.toml\\n- tests/test_doctor.py\\n- tests/test_drive.py\\n- tests/test_ledger.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh: on a fixture tenant with a build-01.started marker naming a dead pid on this host and no build-01.json, attavo doctor --json fails proof no-invocation-lacks-record naming build-01, and holds once build-01.json exists\\n- recover-writes-a-died-record.sh: on the same fixture, attavo drive --recover 1 writes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died, provenance product, with a log beside it, committed by the driver identity with a clean tree, after which proof five holds\\n- died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh: both stage schemas' stop enums name died and hung, the manifest schema declares [drive].stall_after_s, and bin/attavo's STOP_CLASSES names both\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f8b72974-a87c-48c1-9863-33c72a212308\",\"uuid\":\"5d085e24-ce26-45fc-865d-11f0aea30c2a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-17T16:12:01.827Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"## Problem\\n\\nAn invocation that begins and does not end leaves nothing. On 2026-09-17 two build attempts of item #148 died between passing their gates and writing their record: the first with its spawning process, the second under a live one; each left a worktree holding an unrecorded executor commit, no record, no stop, and no line anywhere the product owns. `attavo doctor` held on both, because every proof reads records and a dead invocation writes none; the operator screen rendered the row from the last record and so showed a failed attempt as the whole truth while nothing ran; recovery was three hand-written shell blocks. The product has no primitive for \\\"this invocation began\\\", so nothing can say \\\"and it did not end\\\".\\n\\nRetires: the by-hand recovery of a dead or hung drive (the worktree removed, the branch reset, the events archived by a person); the screen's in-memory notion of a running drive as the only witness that one runs; silence as an outcome.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- bin/attavo\\n- schema/records/build.schema.json\\n- schema/records/verify.schema.json\\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\\n- attavo.toml\\n- tests/test_doctor.py\\n- tests/test_drive.py\\n- tests/test_ledger.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh: on a fixture tenant with a build-01.started marker naming a dead pid on this host and no build-01.json, attavo doctor --json fails proof no-invocation-lacks-record naming build-01, and holds once build-01.json exists\\n- recover-writes-a-died-record.sh: on the same fixture, attavo drive --recover 1 writes build-01.json with status failed and stop class died, provenance product, with a log beside it, committed by the driver identity with a clean tree, after which proof five holds\\n- died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh: both stage schemas' stop enums name died and hung, the manifest schema declares [drive].stall_after_s, and bin/attavo's STOP_CLASSES names both\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\n94:+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_016ZajQpUhLhonwsupaQMzyP\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"=== attest/specs/151/criteria/died-and-hung-are-stop-classes.sh ===\\n#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nfor stage in (\\\"build\\\", \\\"verify\\\"):\\n    enum = json.load(open(f\\\"schema/records/{stage}.schema.json\\\"))[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"stop\\\"][\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"class\\\"][\\\"enum\\\"]\\n    assert \\\"died\\\" in enum and \\\"hung\\\" in enum, (stage, enum)\\ndrive = json.load(open(\\\"schema/manifest.schema.json\\\"))[\\\"properties\\\"][\\\"drive\\\"]\\nassert \\\"stall_after_s\\\" in drive[\\\"properties\\\"], drive\\nPY\\ngrep -q '\\\"died\\\", \\\"hung\\\"' bin/attavo\\n\\n=== attest/specs/151/criteria/doctor-fails-on-an-invocation-without-record.sh ===\\n#!/bin/sh\\nset -e\\nhere=$(pwd)\\ntmp=$(mktemp -d)\\ncd \\\"$tmp\\\"\\ngit init -q -b main .\\ngit config user.email doctor@attavo.invalid\\ngit config user.name \\\"doctor fixture\\\"\\nprintf '[paths]\\\\nrecords = \\\"records\\\"\\\\n\\\\n[drive]\\\\nstall_after_s = 60\\\\n' > attavo.toml\\ngit add attavo.toml\\ngit commit -q -m install\\nmkdir -p records/1\\nsleep 0 &\\ndead=$!\\nwait \\\"$dead\\\"\\npython3 - \\\"$tmp/records/1/build-01.started\\\" \\\"$dead\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, socket, sys\\njson.dump({\\\"at\\\": \\\"2026-09-17T13:16:08Z\\\", \\\"host\\\": socket.gethostname(), \\\"pid\\\": int(sys.argv[2]),\\n           \\\"sha\\\": \\\"0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\\\", \\\"product_version\\\": \\\"fixture\\\"},\\n          open(sys.argv[1], \\\"w\\\"))\\nPY\\ngit add records\\ngit commit -q -m \\\"invocation marker for item 1\\\"\\ncd \\\"$here\\\"\\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \\\"$tmp\\\" > \\\"$tmp/doctor-without.json\\\" || true\\nprintf '{\\\"status\\\": \\\"pass\\\"}' > \\\"$tmp/records/1/build-01.json\\\"\\npython3 bin/attavo doctor --json \\\"$tmp\\\" > \\\"$tmp/doctor-with.json\\\" || true\\npython3 - \\\"$tmp/doctor-without.json\\\" \\\"$tmp/doctor-with.json\\\" <<'PY'\\nimport json, sys\\ndef proof(path):\\n    d = json.load(open(path))\\n    return [x for x in d[\\\"proofs\\\"] if x[\\\"proof\\\"] == \\\"no-invocation-lacks-record\\\"][0]\\nwithout = proof(sys.argv[1])\\nassert without[\\\"holds\\\"] is False, without\\nassert \\\"build-01\\\" in without[\\\"reason\\\"] and \\\"never wrote its record\\\" in without[\\\"reason\\\"], without\\nwith_record = proof(sys.argv[2])\\nassert with_record[\\\"holds\\\"] is True, with_record\\nPY